\n  * October 2018\n\nDOI:10.48550/arXiv.1810.03119\n\nAuthors:\n\nM. Rouzbahani Malayeri\n\nM. Rouzbahani Malayeri\n\n  * This person is not on ResearchGate, or hasn't claimed this research yet.\n\nSara Saeedi Madani\n\n  * Osnabrück University\n\nDariush Kiani\n\n  * Amirkabir University of Technology\n\nImage: Request Full-text Paper PDF\n\nRequest file PDF\n\nTo read the file of this research, you can request a copy directly from the authors.\n\nPreprints and early-stage research may not have been peer reviewed yet.\n\n## Abstract\n\nIn this paper we prove the conjectured upper bound for Castelnuovo-Mumford regularity of binomial edge ideals posed in [23], in the case of chordal graphs. Indeed, we show that the regularity of any chordal graph G is bounded above by the number of maximal cliques of G, denoted by c(G). Moreover, we classify all chordal graphs G for which L(G) = c(G), where L(G) is the sum of the lengths of longest induced paths of connected components of G. We call such graphs strongly interval graphs. Moreover, we show that the regularity of a strongly interval graph G coincides with L(G) as well as c(G).\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nRegularity of binomial edge ideals of Cohen-Macaulay bipartite graphs (https://www.researchgate.net/publication/332689331_Regularity_of_binomial_edge_ideals_of_Cohen-Macaulay_bipartite_graphs)\nciteturn1search8 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: 3 months ago; the number of maximal cliques in it, i.e., the class of k-fan graphs satisﬁes the regularity\n\nupper bound conjecture of Saeedi Madani and Kiani.\nIf for each i∈ {1, . . . , k}, fan on set W i is pure, then F W\n\nk(K n)is said to be a k-pure fan\n\ngraph of K n on W.\n\nExample 3.2. Let G 1 and G 2 be the graphs as shown in the ﬁgure below.\n\n2\n\n1 3\n\n4\n\n6\n\n5\n\nG 1\n\n2\n\n1\n\n3\n\n4\n\n6\n\n5\n\nG 2\n\nLet W={1,2,3} t {4,5}. Then\n\nit can be seen that G 1=F W\n\n2(K 6)\n\nis a 2-pure fan graph while G 2=